UID:3461798373834516622@strava.com
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260304T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260304T200000
DTSTAMP:20260226T084329Z
SUMMARY:Sprints at Priory
DESCRIPTION:Leader: Joe de la Mata\n\nBecause sprints are a prior-ity! 😜
 \n\nThis will be a fun running session starting with a quick warmup followe
 d by a 10-20min set of sprints + an easy-pace recovery 3K run + another 10-
 20min set of sprints + and finished with cool-down stretches to avoid any a
 ches the day after 🔥🔥\n\nSprints sets: this will be a set of exercise
 s in pairs or teams of 3 (depending on the numbers). One person will be spr
 inting towards markers (trees/lamposts) and back while their pals will be d
 oing some exercises for active recovery before swapping over.\n\nSounds int
 ense? Don’t panic\, do it at your own pace. This session will be adapted 
 to everyone’s abilities and adapted exercises will be offered when needed
 .\n\nMeeting point: Priory Park (by the Splash).\n\nMeeting time: 7pm\n\nDu
 ration: ~1hr \n\nKit: high-vis clothing and head-torches recommended. I che
 cked the park and is well lit though but bring your torches.\n\nLiRF: Joe -
  [Phone Number Redacted]\n\nView on Strava: https://www.strava.com/clubs/20
 8705/group_events/3461798373834516622\n\nSynced from Strava Club 208705 on 
 Thu\, 26 Feb @ 8:43 AM
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Leader: Joe de la MataBecause sprints are a pr
 ior-ity! 😜This will be a fun running session starting with a quick warmu
 p followed by a 10-20min set of sprints + an easy-pace recovery 3K run + an
 other 10-20min set of sprints + and finished with cool-down stretches to av
 oid any aches the day after 🔥🔥Sprints sets: this will be a set of exe
 rcises in pairs or teams of 3 (depending on the numbers). One person will b
 e sprinting towards markers (trees/lamposts) and back while their pals will
  be doing some exercises for active recovery before swapping over.Sounds in
 tense? Don’t panic\, do it at your own pace. This session will be adapted
  to everyone’s abilities and adapted exercises will be offered when neede
 d.Meeting point: Priory Park (by the Splash).Meeting time: 7pmDuration: ~1h
 r Kit: high-vis clothing and head-torches recommended. I checked the park a
 nd is well lit though but bring your torches.LiRF: Joe - [Phone Number Reda
